{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nCI, Gerrit, deployment, and infrastructure configuration under `.github/` and `infra/` contain confirmed comment or docstring bloat from the audit pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`. File-specific constraints must survive consolidation.\n\n## Approach\nDelegate remediation to bounded directory/subsystem leaves. Each leaf edits only its declared paths, preserves its Scope requirements, and remains independently reviewable. The change may reword or combine comments; literal-string retention is not required.\n\n## Scope\n- Direct container edits: none; repository edits belong to the leaves.\n- Delegated area: CI, Gerrit, deployment, and infrastructure configuration under `.github/` and `infra/`.\n- Audited-path boundary: paths from retired tickets reached through each leaf's net-active `supersedes` links. Other repository paths are outside this workstream.\n\n## Migration inventory\nAt story completion, the driver reads `rebar list --parent dendritic-irksome-raven --full --output json`, follows each leaf's net-active `supersedes` targets, and compares each source file impact with the replacement Scope and file impact.\n\nThe result is a sorted TSV in a dedicated `session_log` linked `relates_to` this story. Each row is `path<TAB>replacement-leaf-alias<TAB>source-ticket-alias<TAB>scope-count<TAB>file-impact-count`. The completion comment cites the log and records its row count and SHA-256. Passing requires one row per audited path, one replacement leaf per source ticket, both counts equal to 1, no extra replacement paths, and equal expected/Scope/file-impact path sets.\n\n## Semantic preservation oracle\nBefore each leaf closes, an agent that did not author its remediation compares the leaf's base revision, final patchset, Scope, and recorded file impact. That reviewer writes an item-by-item TSV matrix in a `session_log` linked `relates_to` the leaf. Each row is `path<TAB>kind<TAB>scope-item<TAB>before-citation<TAB>after-citation<TAB>verdict<TAB>reviewer-session`, where `kind` is `constraint`, `consumer`, or `bloat-removal`.\n\nEvery Scope constraint and consumer contract needs a PASS row with concrete before/after citations. Every edited comment block needs a `bloat-removal` row confirming that redundant, obvious, duplicated, or historical prose was removed while current non-obvious rationale remained. Semantic equivalence is judged from the cited text and surrounding configuration; exact substring equality is deliberately not an oracle. A missing or FAIL row blocks closure.\n\nBefore review and claim, each current direct leaf records its identified artifact-specific tests, prose-only guard, path-scoped diff check, and untimed worktree-venv `make verify` command. After implementation, it runs those commands at the cited commit before push; any material command change requires a fresh plan review.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every audited source path has exactly one inventory row.\n- [ ] Every inventory row has `scope-count=1`.\n- [ ] Every inventory row has `file-impact-count=1`.\n- [ ] Every Scope constraint has an independent-review PASS row with before/after citations.\n- [ ] Every consumer contract has an independent-review PASS row with before/after citations.\n- [ ] Every edited comment block has a `bloat-removal` PASS row.\n- [ ] Every recorded leaf verification command exits 0 at the cited leaf commit.\n- [ ] The story log records the inventory receipt, leaf command results, and reviewer-log ids.\n\n## Child decomposition\nEach directory/subsystem leaf owns its exact path set. Leaf path sets are disjoint; their union is this workstream's audited-path boundary."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788641582577557001,"uuid":"f4ef07e6-ade9-47b9-859c-4787d650f1c2"}